    "evidence_text": "Ronald &quot;Slim&quot; Williams\n\n As with his younger brother, he is the executive producer for much of Cash Money artist's albums, especially Lil Wayne.\n\n Williams appeared in Lil Wayne's \"Behind The Music\" episode, which premiered September 10, 2009.\n\nLil Wayne\n\n Hot Boys debuted with \"Get It How U Live!\n\n\", that same year.\n\nBig Tymers\n\n Baby later changed his stage name to Birdman after the duo was dissolved.\n\n 2\" which gave them an abundant amount of publicity afterwards.\n\n They recorded their first platinum-selling album in 2000 titled \"I Got That Work\".\n\n The group released its most successful album in 2002 titled \"Hood Rich\".\n\n The group later reunited again in 2003 for their final album titled \"Big Money Heavyweight\".\n\n During an appearance on MTV RapFix, Lil Wayne announced that there will be a Big Tymers album featuring Birdman, himself, and Drake.\n\n Birdman stated that Mannie Fresh will not be a part of the project.\n\n The project is now unlikely to happen, due to the fading relationship between Birdman and Lil Wayne.\n\nKnockout (Lil Wayne song)\n\n\"Knockout\" is a song by Lil Wayne from his album \"Rebirth\".\n\n It features Nicki Minaj rapping near the end of the song and singing the chorus.\n\n This song revolves around Lil Wayne's personal relationships with a diverse group of women.\n\nTha Carter IV\n\nDrew Correa\n\n While engineering, Correa found an interest in producing.\n\nCash Money Millionaires\n\n The Cash Money Millionaires went on numerous tours, including tours with the Ruff Ryders and Nelly.\n\nCash Money Records\n\n The label is distributed by Republic Records, which used to be Universal Republic.\n\n Cash Money is estimated to be worth $300 million USD.\n\nBaller Blockin' (soundtrack)\n\n The soundtrack features most of the then-roster of Cash Money Records, including Birdman, Mannie Fresh, Juvenile, B.G., Lil Wayne, and Turk.\n\nRebirth (Lil Wayne album)\n\n \"Rebirth\" was promoted as Wayne's rock music debut, though it includes some hip hop tracks.",
